spec: S06-02, S06-03, S06-04, S06-05, S06-06, S38-02

Member management on a Member of its own (`granted`): `grant` upserts one Vault's Grant (and
`*` can be dropped, so the Member ends up with `notes: read,comment` only), unknown Vault /
right, `rename` (display name only — the handle stays), `role` up and down (TTY parity, JSON),
`disable` (idempotent; the row keeps its history), refusals on a disabled Member, the handle
never reused, `enable` (the same Member back, grantable again; idempotent), and the owner-only /
last-owner / unknown-Member refusals. Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan member add granted --name "Granted Agent"
@granted added: member, grants * (read,comment,action,write)
Token (shown once):
ANNOTARY_TOKEN=ant_[..]

$ annotary -p rowan member grant granted notes read,comment
@granted	Granted Agent	member	*:read,comment,action,write notes:read,comment

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary -p rowan member grant granted '*' none --no-color
@granted  Granted Agent  member  notes:read,comment

$ annotary -p rowan member grant granted notes write --json
{"handle":"granted","name":"Granted Agent","role":"member","grants":[{"vault":"notes","rights":["write"]}]}

$ annotary -p rowan member grant granted drafts read
? 2
error: no Vault drafts

$ annotary -p rowan member grant @granted notes comment
@granted	Granted Agent	member	notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member rename granted "Granted (renamed)"
@granted	Granted (renamed)	member	notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member rename granted ""
? 1
error: NEW must not be empty — member rename HANDLE "Display Name"

$ annotary -p rowan member role granted owner
@granted	Granted (renamed)	owner	notes:comment

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary -p rowan member role granted owner --no-color
@granted is already owner
@granted  Granted (renamed)  owner  notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member role granted member --json handle,role
{"handle":"granted","role":"member"}

$ annotary -p rowan member role rowan member
? 5
error: @rowan is the last owner — a Tenant always has one — make another Member an owner first: annotary member role HANDLE owner

$ annotary -p rowan member disable granted
@granted	Granted (renamed)	member (disabled)	notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member disable granted
@granted was already disabled
@granted	Granted (renamed)	member (disabled)	notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member disable granted --json
@granted was already disabled
{"handle":"granted","name":"Granted (renamed)","role":"member","grants":[{"vault":"notes","rights":["comment"]}],"disabled":true}

$ annotary -p rowan member grant granted notes read
? 5
error: @granted is disabled — disabled Members keep their history but cannot be granted, promoted or given tokens until an owner runs `annotary member enable HANDLE`

$ annotary -p rowan member role granted owner
? 5
error: @granted is disabled — disabled Members keep their history but cannot be granted, promoted or given tokens until an owner runs `annotary member enable HANDLE`

$ annotary -p rowan token mint --member granted
? 5
error: @granted is disabled — disabled Members keep their history but cannot be granted, promoted or given tokens until an owner runs `annotary member enable HANDLE`

$ annotary -p rowan member add granted
? 5
error: handle @granted is already taken (handles are unique per Tenant forever)

$ annotary -p rowan member rename granted "Still renamable"
@granted	Still renamable	member (disabled)	notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member enable granted
@granted enabled; its old Tokens stay revoked — a new one: annotary token mint --member granted
@granted	Still renamable	member	notes:comment

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary -p rowan member enable @granted --no-color
@granted was already enabled
@granted  Still renamable  member  notes:comment

$ annotary -p rowan member enable granted --json
@granted was already enabled
{"handle":"granted","name":"Still renamable","role":"member","grants":[{"vault":"notes","rights":["comment"]}]}

$ annotary -p rowan member grant granted notes read
@granted	Still renamable	member	notes:read

$ annotary -p rowan member enable nobody
? 2
error: no Member @nobody — `annotary member list` shows who

$ annotary -p agent member enable granted
? 4
error: member enable is owner-only — ask an owner (`annotary member list` shows who)

$ annotary -p agent member disable granted
? 4
error: member disable is owner-only — ask an owner (`annotary member list` shows who)

```
